WEBVTT

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:00.996
your ancestors may have been
Native American or migrated from Asia.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:03.538
If we go inside the tooth
to the pulp cavity,

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:05.413
we may be able to extract the DNA

00:02:05.454 --> 00:02:09.038
and see if your ancestors came
from Egypt or England or both.

00:02:09.871 --> 00:02:11.454
But we're not interested as much

00:02:11.496 --> 00:02:14.538
in your family's
migration history as yours.

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:16.621
And that's where we
go to the tooth enamel,

00:02:16.663 --> 00:02:17.913
what it's made out of,

00:02:17.954 --> 00:02:19.913
to try and find out if a person moved

00:02:19.954 --> 00:02:21.954
and even when they moved.

00:02:21.996 --> 00:02:25.454
And it's based on one simple idea:
that you are what you eat.

00:02:25.496 --> 00:02:27.704
All the minerals
and the elements in the food,

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:30.663
like calcium, oxygen,
which is the O in H2O,